  "memory_contract": "Initialized nonwrapping spans and NUL-terminated strings; arbitrary signed comparison magnitude with exact equality. Nonoverlapping byte copies with writable possibly uninitialized/unaligned destination and arbitrary finite partial-store order on loss. Close modifies only explicitly owned TLS. Exit cannot source-return and is not a Linux extinction receipt.",
  "bounds": {
    "fault_source_and_comparison_steps": 10,
    "fault_max_nonwait_events_including_loss": 11,
    "waiting": "Arbitrary finite waits; no scheduling termination/time bound."
  },
  "nonvacuity": "Arbitrary nonzero string pairs up to combined length158 built with actual allocation/stores for actual source mode symbol; universal fault theorem has no such length limit. Both outcomes, arbitrary waits and nonprefix copy schedule [2,0]. Local owned memory, not whole-program initialization.",
  "tool_profile": "Unchanged pinned CompCert commit 14d616046360a0b2611ebdfc2f98368af402e1f7 (VERSION 3.17), Coq 8.18.0 and OCaml 4.14.1. Source/frontend/extraction correctness remains trusted; no compiler preservation theorem applied to the extended machine.",
